{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Behold, I stand by the water-spring.</b> You should be roused regarding this passage, which is doubled. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said well: the talk of the servants of the Patriarchs before the Holy One, blessed be He, [is more beloved] than the Torah of the children — for the passage of Eliezer is doubled, and many principles of the Torah are given in allusion. And there is no doubt that this is a proof and a great testimony to the preeminence of the Patriarchs, that they themselves are the Chariot. And surely the doubling of the passage is not for naught but for matters, and surely the doubling of the passage is not for naught but for matters that are necessary and indispensable, as I shall explain in the passage. And arouse and open the eye of your intellect, for all these deeds in the success of the mission centered on the spring (עין), and he mentioned this three times in different expressions: this one — ״עין המים״; and he said, ״ואבא היום אל העין״; and he further said, ״ותרד העינה״. And you should reflect on these three expressions: עין, העין, העינה."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The phrase דרז\"ל (דברי רבותינו זכרונם לברכה) resolved as 'our Rabbis of blessed memory.' The bracketed 'is more beloved' reflects the well-known rabbinic dictum being cited; the Hebrew presupposes the comparison without stating it explicitly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:41.341755789Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}